What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/enable
Date:		May 2025
KernelVersion:	6.15
Contact:	qat-linux@intel.com
Description:
		(RW) This attribute can enable KPT by writing a 1 to attribute file enable
		or disable KPT by writing a 0.

		Example usage::

			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/enable
			1
			# echo 1 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/enable

		This attribute is only available for devices that support the
		Key Protection Technology (KPT) feature.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_cnt_per_fn
Date:		May 2025
KernelVersion:	6.15
Contact:	qat-linux@intel.com
Description:
		(RW) This attribute can configure the maximum KPT Symmetric Wrapping Key
		count which ranges from 0 to 128 per Virtual Function (VF)
		can associate by writing value to attribute file swk_cnt_per_fn, or read
		the value from the attribute file. If the configuration value is 0,
		it means no limitation.

		Example usage::

			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_cnt_per_fn
			128
			# echo 128 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_cnt_per_fn

		This attribute is only available for devices that support the
		Key Protection Technology (KPT) feature.

