What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_max_ttl
Date:		May 2025
KernelVersion:	6.15
Contact:	qat-linux@intel.com
Description:
		(RW) This attribute can configure the maximum KPT SWK Time To Live (TTL)
		value which ranges from 0 to 31536000 by writing value to attribute file
		swk_max_ttl, or read the value from the attribute file.
		If the configuration value is 0, it means SWK TTL is eternal.

		Example usage::
			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_max_ttl
			1000
			# echo 1000 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_max_ttl

		This attribute is only available for devices that support the
		Key Protection Technology (KPT) feature.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_shared
Date:		May 2025
KernelVersion:	6.15
Contact:	qat-linux@intel.com
Description:
		(RW) This attribute can configure KPT SWK to be in Shared mode by writing
		a 1 to attribute file swk_shared or None-Shared mode by writing a 0.

		Example usage::
			# cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_shared
			0
			# echo 1 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/<BDF>/qat_kpt/swk_shared

		This attribute is only available for devices that support the
		Key Protection Technology (KPT) feature.
